Hi Zoe,

I'm a contributor to the code for the BART.
The task structure of the BART is a little different from other tasks.
It is three-dimensional in the sense that it includes many pumps within a trial (subject, trial, pump).
Thus, the simulating data also include the three-dimensional structure.
The simulating data indicate the result of each pump for trials and subjects.
Specifically, when I ran the following code,
output <- bart_par4("example", 2000, 1000, 4, 4, inc_postpred = T)
dim(output$parVals$y_pred)
the result was
4000(the number of samples) 3(the number of subjects) 30(the number of trials) 96(the max number of pumps).
I think you can get the information that you want by modifying this data.
If you have anything unclear, please let me know.
Thank you.

Best,
Harhim

